---
import ports from '../../ai-runtime/src/aegis/ports.py?raw';
import domainCode from '../../ai-runtime/src/aegis/domain.py?raw';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import report from '../../public/aegis-data/report.json';
import fixtures from '../../public/aegis-data/fixtures.json';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RoutingLab from './RoutingLab.astro';
import PizzaExplainer from './PizzaExplainer.astro';
import '../styles/pizza.css';
import { architecture, decisions } from '../data/aegis';
import '../styles/aegis.css';
import '../styles/routing.css';
const routingCode = domainCode.split('def evaluate_workload_policy')[1].split('@dataclass(frozen=True)')[0];
const firstNode = architecture[2];
interface Props { portfolioHome?: string; portfolioName?: string; }
const { portfolioHome, portfolioName = 'Portfolio' } = Astro.props;
---
<BaseLayout theme="light" title="Aegis — Local or Cloud?" description="Choose a scenario and discover why an AI task should run locally, in the cloud, or stay blocked. An interactive, plain-language runtime case study.">
  <div class="aegis-app"><div class="aegis-wrap">
    <header class="aegis-topbar"><a href={portfolioHome || "#top"} class="aegis-back">{portfolioHome ? `← ${portfolioName}` : "Aegis"}<span class="aegis-back-divider">/</span> Independent engineering</a><a href="/aegis-data/aegis-source.zip" download class="aegis-source-link">Inspect the source ↗</a></header>
    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
      <section class="aegis-hero" id="top"><div class="aegis-hero-copy"><p class="ag-eyebrow"><span class="ag-dot"></span> INDEPENDENT EXPERIMENT / AI SYSTEMS ENGINEERING</p><h1>Aegis<span>.</span></h1><p class="aegis-full-name">Adaptive Edge AI Agent Runtime</p><h2>One AI task.<br />Local or cloud?</h2><p class="aegis-hero-intro">Your device has limited memory. Your data has privacy rules. The internet may be offline. Explore how a runtime chooses where an AI task should run—and when it should stop.</p><div class="aegis-hero-actions"><a class="ag-button ag-button--primary" href="#routing-lab">Choose a scenario ↗</a><a class="ag-link" href="#runtime-model">Understand the four roles ↓</a></div><p class="aegis-hero-note">Original project · Fictional device conditions · Routing decisions, no model calls</p></div><div class="aegis-hero-visual rl-hero-visual"><p class="ag-eyebrow">EXAMPLE INPUT</p><h3>Private task. 8 GB free.<br />Internet available.</h3><p>The local model can handle the task.<br />Cloud processing is not permitted.</p><div class="rl-hero-result"><span class="ag-eyebrow">ROUTING OUTPUT</span><strong>Run locally ↗</strong></div><p>Change the situation. See the route change.<br />The reason stays visible.</p></div></section>
      <nav class="aegis-section-nav" aria-label="Case study sections"><a href="#routing-lab">Try scenarios</a><a href="#runtime-model">Four roles</a><a href="#pizza-explainer">Pizza explainer</a><a href="#engineering">Optional engineering details</a></nav>
      <RoutingLab />
      <PizzaExplainer />
      <details class="rl-study" id="engineering"><summary>Go deeper: architecture, tests and engineering decisions</summary>
      <section class="ag-section ag-problem" id="problem"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">THE ENGINEERING QUESTION</p><h2>The same task.<br />Different constraints.</h2></div><div><p>A local model keeps data on the device, but needs enough memory and capability. A cloud model needs permission and a working connection. Neither route is always right.</p><p>Telemetry supplies the conditions. Policy rules exclude routes that cannot be used. The scheduler selects an allowed route. An execution adapter would then call the chosen model. The scenario lab demonstrates the first three responsibilities and previews the fourth.</p><div class="ag-proof-row"><div><strong>Python</strong><span>Actual policy evaluation</span></div><div><strong>4 roles</strong><span>Observe · check · choose · run</span></div><div><strong>{report.passed} tests</strong><span>Across the retained runtime</span></div></div></div></section>
        <section class="ag-section" id="architecture"><div class="ag-section-heading"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">02 / THE ARCHITECTURE</p><h2>Replace the adapter.<br />Keep the contract.</h2></div><div class="ag-mode-switch" role="group" aria-label="Explanation depth"><button type="button" data-depth="overview" aria-pressed="true">Overview</button><button type="button" data-depth="deep" aria-pressed="false">Engineering deep dive</button></div></div>
          <p class="ag-section-lead">Select a component. Switch between runtime calls and source-code dependencies to see the difference.</p>
          <div class="ag-architecture-panel" data-meeting-architecture><div class="ag-panel-bar"><span class="ag-mono">PORTS & ADAPTERS</span><div class="ag-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Architecture flow"><button type="button" data-direction="runtime" aria-pressed="true">Runtime calls →</button><button type="button" data-direction="dependency" aria-pressed="false">Dependencies ←</button></div></div>
            <div class="ag-system-layout"><div><div class="ag-system" data-system><svg viewBox="0 0 900 380" aria-hidden="true"><defs><marker id="ag-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></marker></defs><polygon class="ag-core-shape" points="420,58 565,123 565,267 420,332 275,267 275,123"/><path class="ag-system-wire" data-edge="http" data-runtime="M180 225H240L300 155" data-dependency="M180 225H240L300 155" d="M180 225H240L300 155" marker-end="url(#ag-arrow)"/><path class="ag-system-wire" data-edge="inference" data-runtime="M540 225H610L660 95H680" data-dependency="M680 95H660L610 225H540" d="M540 225H610L660 95H680" marker-end="url(#ag-arrow)"/><path class="ag-system-wire" data-edge="policy" data-runtime="M540 225H620L660 158H680" data-dependency="M680 158H660L620 225H540" d="M540 225H620L660 158H680" marker-end="url(#ag-arrow)"/><path class="ag-system-wire" data-edge="scheduler" data-runtime="M540 225H680" data-dependency="M680 225H540" d="M540 225H680" marker-end="url(#ag-arrow)"/><path class="ag-system-wire" data-edge="telemetry" data-runtime="M540 225H620L660 284H680" data-dependency="M680 284H660L620 225H540" d="M540 225H620L660 284H680" marker-end="url(#ag-arrow)"/></svg><div class="ag-source-nodes"><button type="button" data-component="events"><span class="ag-mono">EVENT SOURCES</span>Task + conditions</button><button type="button" data-component="http"><span class="ag-mono">INCOMING ADAPTERS</span>REST / routing API</button></div><div class="ag-core-nodes"><button type="button" data-component="core" aria-pressed="true"><span class="ag-mono">APPLICATION + DOMAIN</span>Runtime orchestration</button><button type="button" data-component="ports"><span class="ag-mono">CORE-OWNED CONTRACTS</span>Application contracts</button></div><div class="ag-adapter-nodes"><button type="button" data-component="inference"><span class="ag-mono">EXECUTION BACKEND / InferenceProvider</span><span data-arch-inference>Model adapter boundary</span></button><button type="button" data-component="policy"><span class="ag-mono">PolicyEngine</span>Admission policy</button><button type="button" data-component="scheduler"><span class="ag-mono">WorkloadScheduler</span><span data-arch-transport>Backend placement</span></button><button type="button" data-component="telemetry"><span class="ag-mono">Clock / DeviceContext</span>Conditions & outcomes</button></div></div><p class="ag-diagram-caption" data-flow-explanation>Runtime calls travel through application-owned ports to replaceable adapters.</p><div class="ag-adapter-controls"><label>Inspect an inference adapter<select data-arch-provider><option value="mock">Simulated model</option><option value="local">Ollama / local model</option><option value="cloud">Cloud-compatible API</option></select></label><p class="ag-small">The scenario lab above stops at the routing decision. Model adapters can be replaced behind the same contract.</p></div><div class="ag-core-boundaries"><button type="button" data-component="policy">Inspect policy engine <span>Eligibility / restrictions</span></button><button type="button" data-component="scheduler">Inspect scheduler <span>Placement / inability</span></button></div><p class="ag-small">Inspecting an adapter does not execute a model. The core and its interfaces stay unchanged.</p></div>
              <aside class="ag-component-inspector" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><p class="ag-eyebrow" data-component-kind>{firstNode.kind}</p><h3 data-component-title>{firstNode.label}</h3><p data-component-summary>{firstNode.summary}</p><dl><dt>BOUNDARY / CONTRACT</dt><dd data-component-port>{firstNode.port}</dd><dt>IMPLEMENTATION</dt><dd data-component-file>{firstNode.file}</dd></dl><p class="ag-deep-only" data-component-detail>{firstNode.detail}</p></aside></div>
            <details class="ag-native-details ag-deep-only"><summary>Inspect the application-owned contracts</summary><Code code={ports} lang="python" theme="github-light" /></details>
          </div>
          <details class="ag-native-details"><summary>Read every component without the interactive explorer</summary><div class="ag-component-guide">{architecture.map(node=><article><h3>{node.label}</h3><p>{node.summary}</p><p class="ag-small">{node.detail}</p></article>)}</div></details>
        </section>



      <section class="ag-section" id="evidence"><div class="ag-section-heading"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">TESTING & EVALUATION</p><h2>Evidence you can rerun.</h2></div><a class="ag-link" href="/aegis-data/report.json" download>Download actual report ↓</a></div><div class="ag-evidence-grid"><div><span class="ag-mono">PYTHON RUNTIME TESTS</span><strong>{report.passed}<small> passed</small></strong><p>{report.failed} failed · Includes routing, reference workflows and adapters</p></div><div><span class="ag-mono">ROUTING EXAMPLES</span><strong>{fixtures.routing_presets.length}<small> presets</small></strong><p>Generated by the Python policy and scheduler</p></div><div><span class="ag-mono">POSSIBLE OUTCOMES</span><strong>3<small> routes</small></strong><p>Local · Cloud · No eligible backend</p></div></div><p class="ag-small">Report generated {report.generated_at} · Python {report.python}. No actual LLM accuracy, hardware utilization or energy benchmark is claimed.</p><details class="ag-native-details"><summary>Inspect the recorded routing decisions</summary><div class="ag-evaluation-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Selected route</th><th>Python rationale</th></tr></thead><tbody>{fixtures.routing_presets.map(item=><tr><th>{item.name}</th><td>{item.result.backend || 'Blocked'}</td><td>{item.result.rationale}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details><details class="ag-native-details"><summary>Inspect the individual pytest results</summary><ul class="ag-test-list">{report.tests.map(test=><li><span>{test.skipped?'SKIP':test.passed?'PASS':'FAIL'}</span><code>{test.name}</code></li>)}</ul></details><details class="ag-native-details"><summary>Read the actual policy and scheduler</summary><Code code={'def evaluate_workload_policy'+routingCode} lang="python" theme="github-light" /></details><div class="ag-limitations"><h3>What this demonstration establishes</h3><ul><li>The Python policy rejects infeasible routes and gives explicit reasons.</li><li>The scheduler applies the selected local/cloud preference among eligible candidates. This is a clear reference strategy, not an optimal cost or performance claim.</li><li>Device readings, model capabilities and latency profiles are fictional inputs.</li><li>The routing lab does not call a model or send a document. No real CPU, GPU, NPU, battery or energy measurement is shown.</li></ul></div></section>
      <section class="ag-section" id="tradeoffs"><p class="ag-eyebrow">ENGINEERING DECISIONS</p><h2>Make the choice explainable.</h2><div class="ag-decisions">{decisions.map((item,index)=><article><span class="ag-mono">ADR {String(index+1).padStart(3,'0')}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.choice}</p><p class="ag-small">{item.tradeoff}</p></article>)}</div><div class="ag-next"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">WHAT I WOULD IMPROVE NEXT</p><h3>Measure real conditions.<br />Calibrate the profiles.</h3></div><p>Use real hardware telemetry and measured model requirements. Evaluate accuracy, latency, energy and cost before changing the scheduling preference. Keep the privacy boundary enforceable when a model is unavailable.</p></div></section>
      <section class="ag-section ag-run-instructions"><div><p class="ag-eyebrow">TAKE IT APART</p><h2>Read it. Run it.<br />Change a backend.</h2><a class="ag-button ag-button--primary" href="/aegis-data/aegis-source.zip" download>Download runtime & tests ↓</a></div><pre><code>uv sync --project ai-runtime
uv run --project ai-runtime pytest ai-runtime/tests
uv run --project ai-runtime uvicorn aegis.http:app \
  --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8011

# Full portfolio, second terminal:
npm run dev</code></pre></section>
      </details>
    </main><footer class="aegis-footer"><a href={portfolioHome || "https://github.com/alexivaner/aegis"}>{portfolioHome ? "← Back to portfolio" : "Source on GitHub ↗"}</a><p>Independent experiment · Fictional conditions · Local draft</p><a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a></footer>
  </div></div>
  <script>
    import { initMeetingArchitecture } from '../scripts/meeting-architecture';
    const root=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-meeting-architecture]');
    if(root) initMeetingArchitecture(root);
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
